WEBVTT

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:03.610
Hey, Roxanne.

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.900
I want to add skills to my equipment.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.150
How do I do that?

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:12.400
Normally you purchase gear that 
comes with skills equipped.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.320
I'm not talking about buying equipment.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.660
How do I add them myself?

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.590
Are you talking about Skill Crystals?

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:19.910
Skill Crystals?

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:25.250
They're formed through the 
accumulation of monster skills.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:25.620
<i>Error

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.890
They're found rarely in labyrinths, 
and when fused with equipment...

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.420
It applies that skill?

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.680
It all depends on the skill of 
the blacksmith fusing the items.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.690
<i>A blacksmith, huh? I'll need that job.</i>

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:40.930
How can I become one?

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:45.690
I'm sorry, but Blacksmith 
is a job unique to dwarves.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:46.880
You aren't eligible.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.440
<i>I can't become one?!</i>

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.440
So I'll have to hire a blacksmith if I 
want to make any equipment with skills.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.120
I wouldn't recommend it.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:01.160
It fails most of the time, 
and blacksmiths dislike direct transactions.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:04.580
Even if you found one, 
there's no telling if you can trust them.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:09.990
Some dwarves have made a fortune by 
pretending the fusion process failed.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.090
I see.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:17.520
They tell their client they failed and make a 
profit selling the equipment with skills later.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.600
Sounds like fusing Skill Crystals 
is a source of a lot of problems.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.930
Yes, Master. Though it's a different story 
if you're on friendly terms with a blacksmith.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.350
Then we'll recruit a blacksmith to our party.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:27.890
What?

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:30.810
Nothing. Mind if I open the window?

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:31.940
That's fine.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.210
Thank you for waiting.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:42.200
<i>Roxanne really is beautiful.</i>

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:45.620
Roxanne, take this leather armor.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.380
Yes, Master. Thank you.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.550
Roxanne, were you able to get it on okay?

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:56.840
<i>Error

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.300
Um...

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.430
<i>Error

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:03.560
<i>I know equipment stretches and 
shrinks to fit the wearer,</i>

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.190
<i>Error

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:06.890
<i>but this is too much.</i>

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:11.830
Thank you.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:14.650
I guess leather armor isn't for women.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:18.950
<i>It looks like the jacket 
doesn't emphasize her figure.</i>

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:22.530
<i>Party Organization, Roxanne.</i>

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.530
<b><i>Select Target</i></b>

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:23.030
<b><i>[Party]
 Kaga Michio
 Roxanne</i></b>

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.990
Shall we get going?

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:27.120
Yes, Master.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:38.080
<b>in the Labyrinth of Another World</b>

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:38.080
<b>Harem</b>

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.710
<b><i>Vale, Vale Plaza</i></b>

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:10.080
Master, aren't we going to the labyrinth?

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:11.550
<i>Teleport.</i>

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.730
Huh? Um...

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:25.560
Huh? What?

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:27.480
Are you okay, Roxanne?

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.990
Master, where are we?

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:39.590
<b><i>Vale Labyrinth, First Floor</i></b>

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:32.360
On the first floor of the labyrinth.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:36.480
But I thought Dungeon Walk could 
only be used inside labyrinths.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:38.590
I used Teleportation magic.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.590
I've never heard of that.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:46.590
It's possible not many others can 
use it, so don't tell anyone.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.850
Master, you're amazing.

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:56.100
Which way should we go?

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.160
Master, if you're looking for monsters, 
there are some nearby to the right.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.360
I can smell them.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:04.780
What? You can?

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:08.270
I don't smell anything unusual.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.100
Is it because you're a wolfkin?

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.790
My nose is exceptionally good, even for a wolfkin.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.380
I'm good at detecting prey.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:18.850
That's amazing.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:21.380
Then could you take us towards the monsters?

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:22.560
Very well.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:25.680
In that case, could you 
lend me a Magic Crystal?

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.510
Magic Crystal? What's that?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.200
Monsters are made of magic power.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.360
When monsters are defeated, 
their magic power gradually accumulates,

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.270
eventually forming a Magic Crystal.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:42.250
Magic Crystals filled with magic power are 
used by guild temples as energy sources.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:44.360
Why do you want me to lend you one?

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:48.930
Because you can't store magic power when you 
defeat monsters unless you have a Magic Crystal.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:52.700
<i>Have I been screwing myself?</i>

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:55.150
Do Magic Crystals sell for a lot?

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:59.590
They're probably the most valuable item 
that can be acquired in labyrinths.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:02.710
Well, they're valuable,

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.630
but you only accumulate a 
tiny amount of magic power at a time.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:09.750
A person sells Magic Crystals only a handful 
of times over the course of their life.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:13.970
Even if you haven't had one 
until now, you didn't lose much.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.770
So it's all right.

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:17.860
Roxanne...

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.690
<i>I made her concerned about me.</i>

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.440
How can we acquire a Magic Crystal?

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:29.030
You can find them in labyrinths or 
purchase empty ones from guilds.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:31.530
Then, let's go buy some later.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.700
<i>Hey, there really was a monster.</i>

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.160
Here I go.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.540
I got it.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.180
A single blow?

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:54.570
Impressive, Master.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:56.390
It's this sword that's impressive.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.350
Don't tell anyone.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.900
Which way next?

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:06.940
Straight ahead.

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:11.340
<i>She's happy?</i>

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:16.410
<i>All right. Let's keep going a little longer.</i>

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:19.160
<b><i>Vale, Vale Restaurant</i></b>

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:21.670
You're the reason we got all of this.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:23.840
Not at all.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:28.300
We were able to defeat so many 
because you're so strong, Master.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.300
No, it's your power that's impressive.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:36.740
Because I was a newcomer to the 
party I used to be part of,

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:39.310
nobody listened to my opinions.

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:42.330
I either watched battles from a distance

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:47.070
or was told to attack inconspicuously 
from behind, but you...

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:51.000
Well... You've got a great power.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.760
We'd better put it to good use.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:56.070
Yes, Master. I'm glad I 
could be useful to you.

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:58.000
Come here and have a seat.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.690
Yes, Master.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.400
From now on, when we enter the room, 
you don't need to wait to be told to sit.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:10.260
Actually, sit as close to me as possible.

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:16.430
I'll try not to climb on top of you 
just because you're sitting next to me.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:21.520
I-I'm fine. I wouldn't mind—

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.610
<i>I like the sound of that.</i>

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:31.360
Can I taste your ears?

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:35.740
What? I-I doubt they taste very good.

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:38.340
I'm just going to play with them.

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:44.480
I'll stop if it hurts or you don't like it.

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:45.750
Let me know right away.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:50.600
Actually, it feels good to have them stroked.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:53.220
<i>Would it be all right to eat them after all?</i>

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:57.640
<i>Anyway, these dog ears 
reminds me of something.</i>

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:01.830
<i>Not sponge cake, but something springier.</i>

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:02.640
<i>Oh, I know.</i>

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:05.560
Do they have grilled seaweed-wrapped 
mochi around here?

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.010
Grilled seaweed-wrapped mochi?

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:10.610
It's a food I like from my homeland.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:13.180
I don't know about around here,

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:14.650
but if you head to the coast,

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.410
you might find people 
grilling fish on the beach.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:20.050
<i>Yeah, that's not quite the same thing.</i>

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:22.910
I see. Maybe I'll try looking for some.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:26.870
Um, Master...

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:30.750
Will you be returning to 
your homeland someday?

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:33.690
<i>My homeland, huh?</i>

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:40.540
<i>I know. I should've been 
thinking about it, but...</i>

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.390
I'm not going back.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:45.920
And besides, I probably can't.

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:49.370
Unfortunately for you,

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:53.520
I won't be disbanding our party 
so I can return to my homeland.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:57.070
Actually, that's not why I asked.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:58.360
I know.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:03.550
Typically people sell slaves 
they no longer need.

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:04.790
It's all right.

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:08.290
I plan on keeping you forever.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:12.750
Yes, Master. Thank you.

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:17.300
But naturally, I do want to 
maximize our party's strength.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:19.540
I'll probably recruit more members.

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:22.050
Yes, Master. It's only natural.

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:27.540
<i>Great. I'll take that to 
mean she consents to [beep].</i>

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:30.770
Two Magic Crystals, please.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:33.180
Are black Magic Crystals acceptable?

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:34.490
<i>Black?</i>

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:38.400
I'd like empty crystals, please.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:40.510
Those would be black Magic Crystals.

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:43.160
They're ten nars per crystal.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:44.570
Roxanne,

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:48.290
thanks for waiting. Here they are.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:52.290
A Magic Crystal's color changes depending 
on the magic power stored inside it.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:57.800
They turn red after defeating ten monsters 
and purple after defeating a hundred.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:00.970
<i>So the color changes with 
each tenfold increase.</i>

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:02.300
Is there a maximum limit?

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:05.720
Apparently, they turn white after 
defeating one million monsters,

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:07.980
but most stop at green, 
which is ten thousand.

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:10.760
It's typical for people to sell 
them once they turn blue,

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:13.270
after defeating 100 thousand monsters.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:16.710
Got it. Then, let's head to the labyrinth.

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:21.660
All right.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:27.640
Impressive. The first floor monsters 
no longer stand a chance against you.

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:30.160
Why don't we head to a higher floor?

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:33.370
You mean it doesn't go down?

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:37.310
It goes upwards because 
the labyrinth is growing.

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:37.880
What?

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:40.550
The labyrinth is growing?

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:44.530
Labyrinths are thought 
to be living creatures.

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:47.600
They lure people to them, 
use monsters to defeat them,

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.560
and feed on their bodies.

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:54.200
There are labyrinths other than this 
one because the labyrinths multiplied.

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:58.940
How do you defeat—no, kill a labyrinth?

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:03.700
The only way is to defeat the boss on 
every level and reach the highest floor.

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:06.310
<i>Sounds like a tough battle.</i>

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:12.130
<i>I should think about acquiring ways 
to attack multiple monsters at once.</i>

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:13.710
<i>Which means...</i>

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:16.400
Are there any spells that attack all targets?

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:22.700
Spells? I've heard such spells exist, 
but I don't know much about them.

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:31.770
<i>If I want to become a Mage, I should 
probably try actually casting spells.</i>

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:36.770
<i>I have Bonus Incantations 
I can use without being a Mage.</i>

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:39.840
<i>I may be able to acquire the Mage job</i>

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:43.190
<i>by casting the attack spells 
in my Bonus Incantations.</i>

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:43.990
<b><i>Gamma Ray Burst</i></b>

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:44.490
<b><i>Meteor Crash</i></b>

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:45.360
<i>I'll start with this one.</i>

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:51.620
<i>In that case...</i>

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:51.540
<i><b>Meteor Crash</b></i>

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:51.540
<i><b>Extreme Drop Dead</b></i>

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:51.540
<i><b>Self-Destruct</b></i>

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:51.540
<i><b>Equivalent Exchange</b></i>

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:51.870
<i><b>Character Settings</b></i>

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:51.870
<i><b>Status
Bonus Equipment
 Bonus Incantations
Bonus Skills</b></i>

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:51.870
<i><b>Gamma Ray Burst</b></i>

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.380
I'm not done yet.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:07.590
<i>I must not have enough MP to cast it yet.</i>

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:11.730
Master, that needle wood 
was our tenth monster.

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:13.640
How is your Magic Crystal looking?

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:16.850
It changed color.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:18.980
What about yours?

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.200
Mine is still black.

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:24.610
Only the person who strikes the 
killing blow gains its magic power.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.740
<i>I didn't notice earlier,</i>

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:30.370
<i>but I have something called 
Crystallization Upgrade as a Bonus Skill.</i>

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:28.110
<i><b>Crystallization Upgrade</b></i>

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.370
<i><b>Character Settings</b></i>

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.370
<i><b>Status
Bonus Equipment
 Bonus Incantations
Bonus Skills</b></i>

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.370
<i><b>Unlock Level Limit</b></i>

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.370
<i><b>Unlock Damage Limit</b></i>

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.370
<i><b>Unlock Party Settings</b></i>

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.370
<i><b>Crystallization Upgrade x32</b></i>

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:32.240
This way.

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:35.150
<i>It's probably a Magic Crystal-related buff.</i>

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:37.960
Right.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.120
x32...

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:41.710
Left.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:42.880
Should be enough.

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:47.760
Roxanne, take a look.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:50.900
Purple? But how?

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:52.180
Don't tell anyone.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:55.230
Master, that's incredible.

00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:58.260
Do you know how much Magic Crystals sell for?

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:02.170
Greens go for ten thousand nars, 
and yellows go for 100 thousand nars.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:06.200
<i>It's not as though I need 
the money right now,</i>

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:08.660
<i>so I guess I'll deactivate 
Crystallization Upgrade.</i>

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:12.580
<b><i>Unlock Damage Limit</i></b>

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:12.580
<b><i>Unlock Party Settings</i></b>

00:14:10.550 --> 00:14:12.580
<i>Unlock Party Settings?</i>

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:15.320
<i>It didn't matter when I was alone,</i>

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:17.290
<i>but now I'm grouping with Roxanne.</i>

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:21.000
<b><i>Unlock Damage Limit</i></b>

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:21.000
<b><i>Unlock Party Settings</i></b>

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:21.000
<b><i>Party Job Settings</i></b>

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:18.870
<i>I should test it out.</i>

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:21.710
<i>Party Job Settings.</i>

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.210
<b><i>Beast Warrior: Lv 6</i></b>

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.210
<b><i>Villager: Lv 8</i></b>

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.210
<b><i>Farmer: Lv 1</i></b>

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.210
<b><i>Warrior: Lv 1</i></b>

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.210
<b><i>Swordsman: Lv 1</i></b>

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.210
<b><i>Explorer: Lv 1</i></b>

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:27.020
<i>So these are Roxanne's jobs.</i>

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:31.220
<b><i>Party Job Settings</i></b>

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:31.220
<i>Kaga Michio</i>

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:31.220
<b><i>Kaga Michio
Roxanne</i></b>

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:31.220
<b><i>Beast Warrior: Lv 6</i></b>

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:31.220
<b><i>Villager: Lv 8</i></b>

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:31.220
<b><i>Farmer: Lv 1</i></b>

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:31.220
<b><i>Warrior: Lv 1</i></b>

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:31.220
<b><i>Swordsman: Lv 1</i></b>

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:31.220
<b><i>Explorer: Lv 1</i></b>

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:31.220
<i>Item Box</i>

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:29.800
<i>Beast Warrior seems to have good effects,</i>

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:31.220
<i>so I'll keep her the way she is.</i>

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:34.450
That just leaves healing.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:37.140
Do you have any healing skills or spells?

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:40.840
The Monk and Priest jobs can use those.

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:44.150
To become one, you must defeat 
monsters with your bare hands.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.400
Your bare hands?

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:49.650
<i>But it seems worth trying out.</i>

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:54.980
Roxanne, could you put away your 
sword and fight bare-handed?

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:55.820
Yes, Master.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:01.790
<i>That said, it'll probably be 
difficult even for the both of us</i>

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:03.840
<i>to defeat monsters bare-handed 
from the get-go.</i>

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:13.970
How was that?

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:17.850
<b><i>Party Job Settings</i></b>

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:17.850
<b><i>Kaga Michio
Roxanne</i></b>

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:17.850
<b><i>Farmer: Lv 1</i></b>

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:17.850
<b><i>Warrior: Lv 1</i></b>

